lunduke-about (0.8-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Force Close copies the app before the confirm dialog, so a refresh
    cannot SIGKILL the wrong process or the process group. pid <= 1 is
    refused, and a confirm is dropped when that app is gone. After the
    dialog, the PID is checked again via /proc (command name and start
    time); a reused PID is not killed. A failed kill reports that call's
    errno.
  * Refresh updates application rows in place, so the list does not blink,
    jump back to the top, or dismiss an open Force Close menu. Rows stay
    put unless the set of apps actually changed.
  * A window closing during refresh no longer aborts on X BadWindow.
    Windows without a PID are listed when they have a title or class, and
    are not given an invented PID (no Force Close). Windows that cannot
    be identified are skipped.
  * Long window titles, including UTF-8, stay titles. The row label
    already ellipsizes.
  * Protected apps (xfwm4, polkit, xfdesktop, xfce4-panel, and the other
    existing names) match the window class exactly. A title that merely
    contains one of those names can still be force-closed.
  * The RAM bar keeps both "RAM Used" and "RAM Free" when a segment is
    too narrow to center the caption inside it.
  * MemAvailable of 0 is honored. MemFree + Buffers + Cached is used only
    when MemAvailable is absent.
  * Opening About This Computer again presents the existing window.
  * Missing-supporters fallback includes Mike Beasley.
  * Meson project version 0.8.4.

 -- LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 16:45:00 +0000

